answers.approach:
scope = choose_one_journey(one_market, few_channels)
// I would not start with a universal optimizer; the control and evidence do not exist yet.
state = build_event_ledger(exposures, decisions, outcomes, consent)
// Preserve timestamps, provenance and uncertainty rather than inventing a perfect customer profile.
objective = negotiate_value(conversion, margin, service_cost, fatigue, long_term_value)
// This is a governance decision expressed mathematically, not a metric the model can discover.
constraints = encode(consent, frequency, eligibility, inventory, channel_ownership)
// Hard constraints should protect customers and operations before optimization begins.
baseline = replay_current_channel_policies(state)
// Quantify contradictions and harm first; otherwise “global lift” has no credible reference point.
policy = learn_constrained_policy(state, causal_tests, uncertainty)
// Delayed, missing and channel-biased feedback make causal experimentation essential.
shadow(policy); then_canary(policy, holdouts, kill_switches)
// Start with suppression and conflict resolution, where downside is bounded and value is testable.
expand_only_if(incremental_value && stable_safety && operating_authority)
// Expect the limiting factor to be budget and decision rights, not model sophistication.
